1
00:00:00,577 --> 00:00:01,747
(Howard:)How about
we split

2
00:00:01,745 --> 00:00:04,745
(Sheldon:)the difference
and discuss why Austria

3
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:08,448
(Sheldon:)was an archduchy
and not just a regular duchy.

4
00:00:08,451 --> 00:00:11,421
(Penny:)Okay, look, here's the thing.
I like pharmaceutical sales--

5
00:00:11,421 --> 00:00:13,721
(Penny:)it's going great-- but I have
an audition for a movie,

6
00:00:13,723 --> 00:00:15,793
(Penny:)and if I get it,
it could screw everything up.

7
00:00:15,792 --> 00:00:19,062
(Sheldon:)Hmm. I know
exactly what you should do.

8
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:21,292
(Sheldon:)Unfortunately,
I cannot tell you.

9
00:00:22,264 --> 00:00:25,034
(Penny:)Well, why?
(sighs)

10
00:00:25,035 --> 00:00:27,035
(Sheldon:)I'm attempting
to turn over a new leaf.

11
00:00:27,037 --> 00:00:28,837
(Sheldon:)Earlier today,
it was pointed out to me

12
00:00:28,838 --> 00:00:31,238
(Sheldon:)that I tend to force my ideas
on people.

13
00:00:32,775 --> 00:00:34,775
(Penny:)You're really
not gonna tell me?

14
00:00:34,778 --> 00:00:38,048
(Sheldon:)No, that train has left
the station.

15
00:00:38,048 --> 00:00:39,218
(Sheldon:)Now, we can
play this

16
00:00:39,215 --> 00:00:40,545
(Sheldon:)one of two ways.

17
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:43,220
(Sheldon:)You can say,
"Trains, tell me more,"

18
00:00:43,219 --> 00:00:44,349
(Sheldon:)or...

19
00:00:44,354 --> 00:00:46,424
(Sheldon:)you can just look at me
like that

20
00:00:46,423 --> 00:00:48,193
(Sheldon:)and I'll start.

21
00:00:52,394 --> 00:00:54,064
(Bernadette:)What's going on
in here?

22
00:00:54,064 --> 00:00:57,064
(Howard:)I am making molecular cocktails.

23
00:00:57,067 --> 00:01:00,867
(Howard:)This sphere is actually
a cosmopolitan.

